      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T18:25:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we really need to pass in protected for compilation?\n\nLooking through the vulkan graphics pipeline and renderpass code, there are currently no references to an attachment\u0027s TextureInfo being protected (or being memoryless for that matter).  I don\u0027t know if this is a bug in the pipeline creation code, or if we don\u0027t actually require protectedness to be set when creating the pipelines.\n\nIf the latter is true, then we presumably are only hitting protected issues here because RenderPassDescs require a full TextureInfo instead of just format+sampleCount, and we assert that protectedness matches what was set on the Caps?  With my proposal to simplify attachments to be just a generic TextureFormat enum value + samplecount, then maybe the need for this change goes away?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 97,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 97,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "dafd32b2fcc19cd485fc6776da67f49cb0074c32",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c9f0ca5_b3c4cb8b",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PublicPrecompile.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 97,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T20:17:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"When the protectedMemory feature is enabled, all pipelines may be recorded in either protected or unprotected command buffers (or both), which may incur an extra cost on some implementations. This can be mitigated by enabling the pipelineProtectedAccess feature, in which case pipelines created with VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_PROTECTED_ACCESS_ONLY_BIT may only be recorded in protected command buffers, and pipelines created with VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_NO_PROTECTED_ACCESS_BIT may only be recorded in unprotected command buffers.\"",
